SHUTDOWN(1)                    P32W Unix                     SHUTDOWN(1)

NAME
       shutdown - warn the users and bring the system down

SYNOPSIS
       shutdown [-r | -h] [now | +minutes] [message ...]

DESCRIPTION
       shutdown is for root. It warns both terminals, ends every
       process and then halts the machine, or with -r restarts it.

       With +minutes it first counts down: once a minute it writes

              *** The system is going down in N minutes ***

       (going down for a reboot with -r), followed by the message,
       to /dev/tty0 and /dev/tty1, with a bell. With now, or no time,
       it goes on at once. Then it:

       -  writes The system is going down NOW (going down for a reboot
          NOW, with -r) to both terminals;

       -  calls sync(2) and sends SIGTERM to init(8), which then
          starts no new getty, so no one can log in;

       -  sends SIGTERM to every other process, waits two seconds,
          and sends SIGKILL to whatever is left;

       -  calls sync(2) again and reboot(2): every mounted
          filesystem is written out and marked clean, and the
          console shows P32W Unix: halted (the emulators exit) or,
          with -r, P32W Unix: rebooting and the boot monitor starts
          (type b to boot again).

       While it counts down, shutdown ignores SIGINT and SIGHUP.
       To cancel, kill it from another terminal (kill(1)).

OPTIONS
       -r     reboot into the monitor afterwards.
       -h     halt afterwards (the default).
       now    no countdown.
       +minutes
              warn each minute for that many minutes first (0 to
              9999; +0 is now).

       The words after these make up the message (at most 199
       characters; more words are dropped).

EXAMPLES
       shutdown now
       shutdown -r +5 new kernel, back in a minute

EXIT STATUS
       Only on failure: 1 if the caller is not root (shutdown: only
       root may do that) or reboot(2) fails; 2 for a + that is not
       followed by a number ("shutdown: +x: bad time").

SEE ALSO
       halt(1), reboot(1), kill(1), sync(1), reboot(2), init(8)

BUGS
       The options must come first and in this order; -r and -h
       cannot be combined. There is no hh:mm time, no -k (warn
       only) and no -c (cancel). A time that is neither now nor
       +minutes is taken as the start of the message.
